! mcp_bootstrap_p45.strap -- THE BREAKDOWN ROUTINE, printed page 45.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.52, header "PAGE NUMBER 45".
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! >>> LINE 10 IS S BRK8, AT 002502.00 -- THE ADDRESS THE BOOT RUN
! HAS BEEN STOPPING AT. <<<
!
! printed p.38 line 17 is "BD,S BRK8" and its binary put S BRK8 at
! 002502.00, seven pages before this one was opened.  With printed
! pp.43 and 44 in the image the PC trail reached half-word 2692,
! which is that address, and stopped: the instruction there was a
! zero.  This is the page that fills it.
!
! AND THE PAGE IS SIGNED.  Line 6-7 read
!
!     -SBRK8,  6 BIT BCD VERSION,  16 BITS BETWEEN
!     -FIELDS.        LARRY LEVY
!
! -- the first author's name this project has transcribed out of the
! MCP listing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "SLC,$" AGAIN, AND IT LANDS ON printed p.44's LAST BIT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 5 is "SLC,$" at 002501.71.  printed p.44's last datum is
! line 33's "VF,234", which rounds to 002501.40 and is 25 bits wide
! (C22-6531 printed p.18: "THE LOCATION COUNTER STANDS AT BIT 25"),
! ending at 002501.71 to the bit.  docs/boot_plan.md A9 recorded
! that address as p.45's opening before p.44 was rendered.
!
! This deck states 002502.00 outright, as every page deck here does;
! the sixteen-bit gap is inside word 002501, which p.44 compiles, so
! mcp_ipl_image()'s contiguity check sees no hole.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE SYMBOLS ARE INDEX REGISTERS, AND THAT TOOK AN ASSEMBLER FIX
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Q X INN, Q X OUT and Q X CF9 are not addresses -- printed p.46
! lines 22-24 define them "QX INN SYN,$1", "QX OUT SYN,$2",
! "QX CF9 SYN,$3" -- and this page uses them in BOTH kinds of field:
! as the J field of "SX,QX INN,Q SAV1" and as the INDEX of
! "Q KSIZ(QX INN)".
!
! C22-6531 printed p.31 is why one symbol can do both:
!
!   "the meaning of the newly defined symbol A is that whenever A is
!    written in the program, the effect is the same as if Y had been
!    written.  THE MEANING OF SYN IS ALWAYS ONE OF EXACT
!    SUBSTITUTION."
!
! and "$1" was already context-dependent in this assembler -- the
! register number 1 in an I or J field, the bit address 000021.00 in
! an address field, which is C22-6531's own worked example.  Storing
! a SYN's VALUE loses that: 000021.00 in a four-bit register field
! is 0, not 1.  strap_asm.py now remembers the substitution.  LINE
! 19 IS THE ROW THAT SAYS SO: it prints 81, and 80 is what the old
! assembler gave.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND A dds TRAVELS THROUGH A SYN TOO
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 20 and 22 are "KF,Q CMA" and "KF,Q BLNK" with NO data
! description written, and both print 006600 -- a length of six and
! a byte size of six.  Those are the table character's properties,
! and the same sentence of C22-6531 printed p.31 carries them:
! "data properties (dds) associated with Y and its bit address or
! integer classification are TRANSFERRED to A."
!
! strap_asm.py had been ACCEPTING a dds on a SYN and silently
! dropping it, which is the wrong-output-no-error shape this project
! keeps finding.  It now keeps it, and these two rows are the check.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE MORE SWAPs, AND THEY ARE ON THE ERROR PATH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 47-49 are "SWAPI,1,QX INN,Q SAV1" and its two fellows,
! commented "-RESTORE INDEXES BUT SAVE PRESENT VALUES AT QBRK8".
! They sit under Q 2BIG, which line 24's "CBRZ,QX CF9,Q 2BIG"
! reaches when a card field is longer than the output slot -- the
! OVERSIZED-FIELD path, ending in line 52's "-ERROR RETURN".
!
! So SWAP now has SIX documented callers: two on printed p.40, one
! on p.43, three here.  The model still refuses the instruction.
! WHETHER THIS PAGE EXECUTES ONE IS A QUESTION THE BOOT RUN
! ANSWERS, not this deck -- see docs/boot_plan.md.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 30 IS listing_typography.md 13 IN A NEW SHAPE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The row prints "3C* C02520.00    C02516.50 C0" at 900 dpi.  THREE
! separate zeros come out as C in one row -- in the LINE NUMBER
! (30), in the LOCATION (002520) and in the trailing byte -- so this
! is a per-ROW artifact and not the per-glyph one 13 has recorded
! until now.  The byte is 00 and the statement is a plain "B,Q BL";
! the decode says the same thing, because printed p.43 line 50's
! "B,Q CHK" prints 002454.10 00 and an operation of 1100 is the
! conditional branch line 21 prints as C2.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.
!
! (2) THE STAND-IN SYNs CARRY A dds WHERE THE LISTING'S ROWS PROVE
!     ONE.  Q CMA and Q BLNK are written "SYN(BU,6,6)" because lines
!     20 and 22 print 006600 and nothing else can put it there.  The
!     other stand-ins carry none, because no row on this page shows
!     one.
!
! (3) NOTHING ELSE.  "0.($15)", "1.($15)" and "2.($15)" are written
!     as the listing writes them, trailing period and all.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE FOURTEEN STAND-INS, read off THIS page's binary
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   QX INN  $1          lines 10, 13, 14: the J field
!   QX OUT  $2          lines 11, 15
!   QX CF9  $3          lines 12, 16
!   Q KSIZ  6           line 19's address 000000.06 and byte size 6
!   QW CF9  002555.00   line 16
!   QCOUNT  002556.37   line 18
!   Q CMA   002556.31   line 20, with the dds note (2) gives
!   Q BLNK  002556.61   line 22, likewise
!   Q SKIP  002556.00   line 36 -- a 19-bit address field, so this
!                       page pins it only to the word
!   Q SAV1  002547.00   lines 10, 41, 47
!   Q SAV2  002550.00   lines 11, 42, 48
!   Q SAV3  002551.00   lines 12, 43, 49
!   Q SAV4  002552.00   line 50
!   Q SAV6  002554.00   line 51
!
! THE GAP BETWEEN Q SAV4 AND Q SAV6 IS TWO WORDS AND LINE 50 FILLS
! IT EXACTLY: "TI,2,$L,Q SAV4" prints a count of 2 in its J field,
! and 002552 + 2 = 002554.  A count of one would leave 002553
! unwritten and a count of three would overwrite Q SAV6 -- so the
! page states its own extent, and printed p.46 line 20 names 002553
! "-STORE $R".

        SLC, (8)2502.0

QXINN   SYN, $1
QXOUT   SYN, $2
QXCF9   SYN, $3
QKSIZ   SYN, 6
QWCF9   SYN, (8)2555.0
QCOUNT  SYN, (8)2556.37
QCMA    SYN(BU,6,6), (8)2556.31
QBLNK   SYN(BU,6,6), (8)2556.61
QSKIP   SYN, (8)2556.0
QSAV1   SYN, (8)2547.0
QSAV2   SYN, (8)2550.0
QSAV3   SYN, (8)2551.0
QSAV4   SYN, (8)2552.0
QSAV6   SYN, (8)2554.0

        SLC, (8)2502.0

! ---- save, and set up IN, N, OUT and the character count ----------
SBRK8   SX, QXINN, QSAV1            ! line 10 -SAVE INDEX REGISTERS
        SX, QXOUT, QSAV2            ! line 11
        SX, QXCF9, QSAV3            ! line 12
        LV, QXINN, 0.($15)          ! line 13 -INITIALIZE IN
        LC, QXINN, .32($15)         ! line 14 -INITIALIZE N
        LV, QXOUT, 1.($15)          ! line 15 -INITIALIZE OUT
        LX, QXCF9, QWCF9            ! line 16 -COUNT CHARS IN STORED
        CM0000(BU,18,8), 1.32($15)  ! line 17 -INITIALIZE FIELD COUNT
        L(BU,18+QKSIZ), QCOUNT, 64  ! line 18

! ---- the character loop -------------------------------------------
QNEXT   LF(V+I)(BU,QKSIZ), QKSIZ(QXINN)   ! line 19 -LOAD INPUT CHAR.
                                           !           STEP X
        KF, QCMA                    ! line 20 -IS THIS A COMMA
        BAE, QIFC                   ! line 21
        KF, QBLNK                   ! line 22 -IS THIS A BLANK
        BAE, QSTEP                  ! line 23
        CBRZ, QXCF9, Q2BIG          ! line 24 -TEST FOR OVERSIZED
                                     !           FIELD
        SF(V+I)(BU,QKSIZ), QKSIZ(QXOUT)   ! line 25 -STORE CHAR. STEP X
QSTEP   CB, QXINN, QNEXT            ! line 26 -TEST FOR LAST INPUT
                                     !           CHAR

! ---- the last field, and the blanks that pad it -------------------
        M+1(BU,18), 1.32($15)       ! line 27 -COUNT LAST FIELD
QBL     CBZ, QXCF9, QRSTR           ! line 28 -STORE R.H. BLANKS AT
                                     !           END OF LAST FIELD
        SF(V+I)(BU,QKSIZ), QKSIZ(QXOUT), 64   ! line 29 -IF NECESSARY
        B, QBL                      ! line 30 -- see the note above;
                                     !           the listing prints
                                     !           the byte with a C

! ---- a comma closes a field ---------------------------------------
QIFC    M+1(BU,18), 1.32($15)       ! line 32 -COUNT THIS FIELD
        CBRZ, QXCF9, QREDY          ! line 33 -TEST FOR SHORT INPUT
                                     !           FIELD
QZERO   SF(V+I)(BU,QKSIZ), QKSIZ(QXOUT), 64   ! line 34 -STORE R.H.
        CBR, QXCF9, QZERO           ! line 35 -  BLANKS AFTER SHORT
                                     !           FIELD
QREDY   V+, QXOUT, QSKIP            ! line 36 -SKIP TO BEG OF NEXT
                                     !           OUTPUT FIELD
        KF(BU,18), 1.32($15), 64+QKSIZ   ! line 37
        BZAH, QRSTR                 ! line 38
        CB, QXINN, QNEXT            ! line 39 -TEST FOR LAST INPUT
                                     !           CHAR

! ---- the normal return --------------------------------------------
QRSTR   LX, QXINN, QSAV1            ! line 41 -RESTORE INDEX REGISTERS
        LX, QXOUT, QSAV2            ! line 42
        LX, QXCF9, QSAV3            ! line 43
        B, 2.32($15)                ! line 44 -NORMAL RETURN

! ---- the oversized-field error path, and the three SWAPs ----------
Q2BIG   M+1(BU,18), 1.32($15)       ! line 46 -COUNT THIS FIELD
        SWAPI, 1, QXINN, QSAV1      ! line 47 -RESTORE INDEXES BUT
        SWAPI, 1, QXOUT, QSAV2      ! line 48 -  SAVE PRESENT VALUES
        SWAPI, 1, QXCF9, QSAV3      ! line 49 -  AT QBRK8
        TI, 2, $L, QSAV4            ! line 50 -SAVE $L AND $R
        SX, $15, QSAV6              ! line 51
        B, 2.($15)                  ! line 52 -ERROR RETURN

        END, SBRK8

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND THREE LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location that
! every page since printed p.3 carries: lines 5 ("002501.71 *"),
! 26 ("002515.00 *") and 46 ("002530.00 *").
